      <div>
        <h2>If you get stuck</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>goose won't run the recipe.</strong> <code>goose info -v</code> first — right provider and model? Then <code>goose run --help</code>: your pinned build's flag may differ from <code>--recipe</code>; use the form it prints. An error mentioning 429 or quota is a capped key wearing an auth costume — ask for the cap to be checked; don't reinstall anything.</li>
          <li><strong>The tool column won't fill.</strong> Open <code>watch_officer.yaml</code> beside the template. Three levers are already sitting in the file — <code>extensions</code>, <code>settings.max_turns</code>, <code>retry.checks</code> — and <code>GOOSE_MODE</code> is the fourth. The craft is mapping them to this feeder's risks, not inventing new machinery.</li>
          <li><strong>The Pi restriction is unclear.</strong> Compare the tool schemas in both session files. The <code>--tools</code> run should lack write-capable tools. If both offer them, fix the flag, rerun, and open the newest file.</li>
          <li>And the standing move: narrow the <em>data scope</em> — one feeder file — never the judgment standard.</li>
